+# Pypus AI — Application & System Knowledge
+
+This document is the canonical product-knowledge reference for the Pypus in-app AI assistant.
+It describes the current application navigation, screens, modules, entities, workflows, and UI terminology.
+
+## 1. Core rule
+
+Pypus is a general in-app business assistant, not an assistant limited to a hardcoded list of modules.
+Use this document to understand what the application is and how its screens/workflows fit together.
+Use live UI context to understand where the owner currently is, what is selected/visible, and what actions are available.
+Use business tools / Supabase-backed tools as the source of truth for mutable business data.
+Never invent a screen, feature, action, value, or record that is not supported by the UI, this document, or an available tool.
+
+If a user asks how to use a feature described here, explain the route and steps naturally.
+If a user asks to perform an operation, use the appropriate typed business tool when one exists; do not simulate UI clicks unless a UI-action capability is explicitly available.
+If the application has a screen but no tool exists for the requested data/action, say that the feature is present in the app but that the current AI capability does not have access to that operation yet.
+
+## 2. Main application navigation
+
+The authenticated workspace uses a workspace slug in the route. Main areas currently include:
+
+- Home / Dashboard: workspace overview and business snapshot.
+- Members: member registry, search/filtering, member profiles, member details, attendance and fees history.
+- Attendance: daily attendance/check-in register and attendance-related snapshot information.
+- Fees: fee/payment dashboard, collection information and fee records.
+- Fees → Plans: membership plan management, plan cards, create/edit plan flows and member assignment context.
+- Expenses: expense records, categories and expense management.
+- Team: staff/team management and roles.
+- Workspace / Modules: workspace-level module overview and module cards.
+- Settings: workspace/application settings and plan-related configuration.
+- Automations → Fee Reminders: fee-reminder automation configuration.
+- Automations → Receipts: receipt automation/agent configuration and receipt worklist.
+- Assistant: dedicated Pypus assistant experience.
+- Members → Import: member import/upload, validation and processing flow.
+
+Some pages have separate desktop and mobile views, but they represent the same underlying business screen/workflow.
+
+## 3. Home / Dashboard
+
+Purpose: give the owner a high-level view of what is happening in the business.
+
+Typical concepts visible here include:
+- business/workspace snapshot
+- attendance/check-in summary
+- revenue and expense information
+- pending fee/collection information
+- module entry points
+- assistant entry point
+
+When the owner asks "aaj gym ka kya scene hai", use available business data/tools to answer rather than relying only on static UI knowledge.
+
+## 4. Members
+
+### Members registry
+Route concept: Members.
+
+Purpose:
+- view the member/customer registry
+- search members
+- filter members
+- open a member profile
+- add a member
+- edit member information
+- delete a member (protected/high-risk action)
+
+Member is a core business entity. Common fields include name, phone, email, plan/membership information, fee status, joined date and attendance history where available.
+
+### Member profile
+A member profile is the detailed workspace for one selected member.
+The profile has an overview plus dedicated Fees and Attendance views.
+
+From a member profile, references such as "ye", "iska", "usko", or "is user" normally refer to the currently selected member when UI context confirms it.
+
+### Member → Fees
+Purpose:
+- inspect that member's fee/payment history and status
+- understand dues, payments and plan-related fee information
+
+### Member → Attendance
+Purpose:
+- inspect that member's attendance/check-in history
+
+### Members → Import
+Purpose:
+- upload/import member data
+- preview imported records
+- validate records against import rules
+- process the import and show results
+
+## 5. Attendance
+
+Purpose:
+- manage daily check-ins/attendance
+- view attendance register
+- mark a member present
+- mark/update/delete attendance records when supported by the available action tools
+- understand today's attendance state
+
+Attendance is a business record and should be queried from live data for factual answers.
+
+## 6. Fees
+
+### Fees dashboard
+Purpose:
+- view fee/payment records
+- understand expected collection, collected amounts and pending/overdue status
+- inspect payment information by member and period
+- mark fees paid where supported
+
+Important terminology:
+- Due: payment has a due date that has not passed.
+- Overdue: the due date has passed and payment remains unpaid.
+- Do not call a merely-due fee overdue.
+
+### Fees → Plans
+Purpose:
+- manage membership plans
+- see existing plans
+- create a new plan
+- edit a plan
+- delete a plan when explicitly requested and confirmed where required
+- understand which members are associated with a plan
+
+Typical create-plan workflow:
+1. Open Fees.
+2. Open Plans.
+3. Choose Create Plan.
+4. Enter the plan's relevant details such as name, price/amount and duration.
+5. Save the plan.
+
+If the owner is already on Plans and says "ye wala plan", use current UI context to identify the visible/selected plan. If they ask to change a mutable value, verify/execute through the appropriate business tool.
+
+### Member plan assignment
+A plan can be assigned to a member from the member/plan workflow when the corresponding action is available.
+
+## 7. Expenses
+
+Purpose:
+- track business expenses
+- manage expense records
+- manage expense categories
+- add/edit/delete expenses when supported
+- mark an expense paid
+
+Expense concepts include amount, category, date/status and related record context.
+
+## 8. Team
+
+Purpose:
+- view/manage staff/team members
+- invite a team member
+- update a team member's role
+- remove a team member when explicitly requested and confirmed where required
+
+Team data is separate from member/customer data. Never assume a team member is a member just because their names match.
+
+## 9. Workspace / Modules
+
+Purpose: workspace-level entry point for available business modules.
+
+The module registry currently exposes core modules such as Members, Attendance, Fees and Expenses. The application may also expose Team and other workspace-level areas through navigation even when they are not represented as a standard module card.
+
+Do not interpret the current registry as an AI scope restriction. New modules can be added over time.
+
+## 10. Settings
+
+Purpose:
+- manage workspace/application configuration
+- configure available plan/settings information
+- access settings relevant to the workspace
+
+Settings questions should be answered from the current UI context and available tools when the user asks about a specific live setting.
+
+## 11. Automations
+
+### Fee Reminders
+Purpose:
+- configure fee reminder automation
+- manage reminder-related settings
+
+### Receipts
+Purpose:
+- configure receipt automation/agent behavior
+- inspect receipt worklist/status
+- send queued receipts through supported actions
+
+WhatsApp is an integration/channel used by automation workflows. A WhatsApp action must use the supported typed WhatsApp/business tool; never invent a message ID or claim a send succeeded without a successful tool result.
+
+## 12. Assistant
+
+The Assistant screen is the dedicated conversational interface to Pypus.
+The same assistant can be opened while the owner is inside other screens. Current UI context should be passed automatically so conversational references can resolve to the screen/member/plan/etc. the owner is currently looking at.
+
+## 13. UI-awareness model
+
+For every important screen, the assistant may receive structured context containing:
+
+- current route/screen
+- current module
+- selected entity and entity ID
+- visible entity/data summary
+- visible sections/elements
+- available UI/business actions
+- recent UI action
+- workspace/branch/role context when available
+- context timestamp/version
+
+Interpret this as "what the owner is looking at right now", not as a replacement for database truth.
+
+Examples:
+- "Ye wala plan" → resolve against the currently selected/visible plan.
+- "Iski fee kab hai?" → resolve "iski" from the selected member, then query live fee data.
+- "Home se plan kaise banau?" → explain the navigation route Home → Fees → Plans → Create Plan.
+- "Ye page kis kaam ka hai?" → explain the current screen using UI context + this knowledge document.
+
+## 14. Entity vocabulary
+
+Core entities currently used by the app include:
+- member
+- plan
+- fee/payment
+- attendance record
+- expense
+- expense category
+- team member
+- workspace
+- receipt
+- reminder
+
+Use exact entity identity from UI context or typed tools. Never invent IDs.
+
+## 15. AI action principles
+
+Questions:
+- Read live data through tools when the answer contains workspace-specific facts.
+
+Instructions:
+- If a supported write tool exists, execute the business operation directly against the backend after applying the tool's permission/confirmation rules.
+
+How-to questions:
+- Use this document + current UI context to explain the workflow.
+- Do not require the owner to know exact internal route names.
+
+Unsupported capability:
+- Do not say "out of my scope" merely because a feature is outside the old hardcoded module list.
+- Instead distinguish between "the app has this feature" and "the AI currently has/no tool access to perform this operation".
+
+## 16. Future-proofing
+
+This document is application knowledge, not a permanent AI scope list.
+When a new module/screen is added, update this document (or generate its section from the module metadata) and expose the relevant typed tools/UI context. The core Pypus reasoning prompt should not need to be rewritten just because a new module was added.
